{
  "observed": "Current RecognitionPurchaseEvidence exposes forMatches and forReference, but no forSelfie entrypoint. A bounded app/routes search found no caller of RecognitionPurchaseEvidence. Nine current-baseline operator tests report available=false and no recognition request. Existing helper plus forMatches produces the recorded expected results in all nine cases.",
  "priority": "The previous authorship-transfer atom independently passed and authorize-next is authorized. The approved next experiment is fresh generation for an unfinished product atom. Querying registered selfie histories is the missing producer connection into the completed purchase-evidence resolver. Direct discount application would additionally require unresolved same-person and location eligibility decisions; automating decomposition would not perform the approved new-task test.",
  "manual": "Selecting the atom and preparing requirements, tests, oracle, sources and driver template remain manual. Installed machinery must author and process the product candidate.",
  "limits": "Internal service entrypoint only. No claim that checkout invokes it yet or that probability establishes identity. Existing cases use controlled fixtures and intercepted provider HTTP. This is new business capability, classified product progress; no new autonomous responsibility is claimed."
}

{
  "chosen": "Connect the actual helper query to the existing resolver in one bounded service entrypoint.",
  "before": "Previous atom reconstructed existing code. This entrypoint is absent in current code and all nine cases.",
  "alternative": "Another replay cannot test new-task transfer. Wiring checkout now would combine lookup with unresolved identity/location qualification and discount application.",
  "falsifier": "Admission withholds if this connection lacks practical value or priority; generation failure is preserved and cannot be replaced by assistant-written product code."
}

